('sofer-inchiriere','en','109','109','Studies show that at a blood alcohol level of 0.5‰, which may be produced by consuming two glasses of wine:','[{"key":"a","text":"the risk of an accident begins"},{"key":"b","text":"the risk of an accident is multiplied 10 times"},{"key":"c","text":"the risk of an accident is multiplied by 2 times"},{"key":"d","text":"the risk of an accident is multiplied by 35 times"}]','c','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','110','110','Studies show that at a blood alcohol level of 0.8 ‰:','[{"key":"a","text":"the risk of an accident begins"},{"key":"b","text":"the risk of an accident is multiplied 10 times"},{"key":"c","text":"the risk of an accident is multiplied by 2 times"},{"key":"d","text":"the risk of an accident is multiplied by 35 times"}]','b','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','111','111','Studies show that at a blood alcohol level of 1.2 ‰:','[{"key":"a","text":"the risk of an accident begins"},{"key":"b","text":"the risk of an accident is multiplied 10 times"},{"key":"c","text":"the risk of an accident is multiplied by 2 times"},{"key":"d","text":"the risk of an accident is multiplied by 35 times"}]','d','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','112','112','Alcohol consumption may have the following effects:','[{"key":"a","text":"decrease in reaction time"},{"key":"b","text":"judgment becomes prompt and selective"},{"key":"c","text":"reduction of visual field"},{"key":"d","text":"widening the field of vision"}]','c','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','113','113','Alcohol consumption may have the following effects:','[{"key":"a","text":"improves gesture accuracy"},{"key":"b","text":"increased reflexes"},{"key":"c","text":"increases reaction time"},{"key":"d","text":"increases thinking ability"}]','c','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','114','114','Alcohol consumption may have the following effects:','[{"key":"a","text":"incorrect assessment of speeds"},{"key":"b","text":"increasing analytical capacity"},{"key":"c","text":"increasing driver vigilance"},{"key":"d","text":"reducing the risk of an accident"}]','a','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','115','115','Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"key":"a","text":"alcohol is absorbed into the body very quickly but its elimination takes a much longer time"},{"key":"b","text":"alcohol is absorbed slowly into the body but eliminated quickly"},{"key":"c","text":"alcohol is eliminated from the body only after 14 hours of sleep"},{"key":"d","text":"the time it takes for alcohol to be absorbed into the body is equal to the time it takes for it to be eliminated"}]','a','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','116','116','The order of intervention for providing first aid to a person who has suffered multiple injuries is:','[{"key":"a","text":"alerting authorities, stopping bleeding, clearing the airway and immobilizing fractures"},{"key":"b","text":"clearing the airway, stopping bleeding and immobilizing fractures"},{"key":"c","text":"immobilizing fractures, clearing the airway and stopping bleeding"},{"key":"d","text":"stopping bleeding, clearing the airway and immobilizing fractures"}]','b','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','117','117','Before proceeding to transport victims of a traffic accident, you must make sure:','[{"key":"a","text":"that evidence from the accident scene was preserved"},{"key":"b","text":"that respiratory and circulatory functions are ensured"},{"key":"c","text":"that the vehicle used for the transport ensures the necessary comfort"},{"key":"d","text":"that the victim will be assisted during the journey by a competent person"}]','b','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','118','118','How should a wounded person with spinal injuries be placed in a means of transport?','[{"key":"a","text":"in a sitting position with your back and head supported"},{"key":"b","text":"in the back seat of a car to ensure a horizontal body position"},{"key":"c","text":"it is advisable not to move him until the ambulance arrives"},{"key":"d","text":"lying on one side in the lateral safety position"}]','c','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','119','119','What should you keep in mind when periodically checking and restoring tire pressures?','[{"key":"a","text":"these operations must be carried out by specialized and authorized personnel in this regard"},{"key":"b","text":"periodic inspection should be carried out at least once a year or after an intervention on the running system"},{"key":"c","text":"pressure restoration operations should be carried out \"cold\""},{"key":"d","text":"pressures should be corrected periodically depending on the wear and tear of the tires"}]','c','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','120','120','What should you keep in mind when periodically checking and restoring tire pressures?','[{"key":"a","text":"pressures should be established and adapted periodically, in accordance with the categories and road conditions specific to the routes that will be routinely traveled"},{"key":"b","text":"pressures should be established and adjusted periodically, depending on the wear and tear of the tires"},{"key":"c","text":"the pressures must comply with the recommendations specified by the manufacturer"},{"key":"d","text":"these operations must be carried out by specialized and authorized personnel in this regard"}]','c','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','121','121','What will be written on the note that is attached next to the tourniquet applied to a person with severe bleeding, injured in a traffic accident?','[{"key":"a","text":"how the hemorrhage occurred and the procedure applied to stop it"},{"key":"b","text":"the hour and minute when the tourniquet was applied"},{"key":"c","text":"the name, surname and contact details of the person who applied the tourniquet"},{"key":"d","text":"the victim''s blood type, first and last name, and age"}]','b','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','122','122','In which of the following situations is the exercise of the right to drive vehicles on public roads suspended:','[{"key":"a","text":"exceeding the maximum speed allowed by law on the road section by more than 50 km/h"},{"key":"b","text":"driving a vehicle without a tachograph chart and/or failure to comply with driving time"},{"key":"c","text":"exceeding by more than 30 km/h the maximum speed allowed by law on the road sector on which you are driving and for the category to which the vehicle you are driving belongs"},{"key":"d","text":"exceeding by more than 40 km/h the maximum speed allowed by law on the road sector on which you are driving and for the category to which the vehicle you are driving belongs"}]','a','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','123','123','Factors that reduce driving ability are:','[{"key":"a","text":"drugs, correct driving position and good eyesight"},{"key":"b","text":"fatigue, alcohol and avoiding driving at night"},{"key":"c","text":"fatigue, alcohol, drugs"},{"key":"d","text":"proper rest, alcohol and medication"}]','d','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','124','124','Which of the following factors directly and decisively influences braking distance?','[{"key":"a","text":"engine efficiency and maximum torque developed by it"},{"key":"b","text":"speed limiter type"},{"key":"c","text":"tire size and profile"},{"key":"d","text":"vehicle speed"}]','d','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','125','125','Which of the following factors directly and decisively influences braking distance?','[{"key":"a","text":"cardan transmission and planetary gears"},{"key":"b","text":"compression ratio"},{"key":"c","text":"distribution system"},{"key":"d","text":"vehicle weight"}]','d','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','126','126','Which of the following factors directly and decisively influences braking distance?','[{"key":"a","text":"connecting rod-crank mechanism"},{"key":"b","text":"steering angle"},{"key":"c","text":"tire-road adhesion"},{"key":"d","text":"vehicle maneuverability"}]','c','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','127','127','Stopping distance means:','[{"key":"a","text":"the distance traveled between the moment the obstacle is detected and the brake pedal is pressed"},{"key":"b","text":"the distance traveled from the moment the brake pedal is pressed until stopping"},{"key":"c","text":"the distance traveled from the moment the braking system comes into operation until it stops"},{"key":"d","text":"the sum of the reaction distance and the braking distance"}]','d','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','128','128','The main cause of accidents, among those listed, is:','[{"key":"a","text":"fatigue while driving"},{"key":"b","text":"poor condition of the public road"},{"key":"c","text":"speeding over the permitted limits"},{"key":"d","text":"technical failures of the lighting system"}]','c','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','129','129','Why is it necessary to maintain a much greater distance from vehicles in front after a heavy rain:','[{"key":"a","text":"because it increases the efficiency of the braking system in these conditions"},{"key":"b","text":"because the stopping distance is much greater"},{"key":"c","text":"because the temperature of the rims increases"},{"key":"d","text":"because the tire-road adhesion decreases"}]','b','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','130','130','To control a skid, you will need to:','[{"key":"a","text":"brake the vehicle progressively until it stops"},{"key":"b","text":"do not accelerate, brake or turn the wheels in the direction of rotation of the vehicle"},{"key":"c","text":"do not accelerate, brake progressively and counter-steer the wheels in the opposite direction to the vehicle''s rotation"},{"key":"d","text":"progressively turn the steering wheel until the steering wheels become parallel to the longitudinal axis of the vehicle"}]','c','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','131','131','How is a level crossing with a current railway without barriers or semi-barriers signalized?','[{"key":"a","text":"with one of the signs \"Level crossing with single track\" or \"Level crossing with double track\" and the sign \"Yield the crossing\" or \"Stop\" for single track or double track, respectively"},{"key":"b","text":"with one of the signs \"Single-track level crossing, without barriers\" or \"Double-track level crossing, without barriers\" accompanied by the \"Stop\" sign"},{"key":"c","text":"with the \"Give way\" indicator and light and sound warning devices"},{"key":"d","text":"with warning signs \"Railway level crossing without barriers\" and three additional panels placed at a distance of 50 meters between them"}]','b','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','132','132','Who is responsible for preparing the vehicle for the ride?','[{"key":"a","text":"personnel with functions that contribute to road safety"},{"key":"b","text":"the driver"},{"key":"c","text":"the person designated to permanently and effectively manage the transport activity the road transport activity"},{"key":"d","text":"transport coordinator"}]','b','[]'),
('sofer-inchiriere','en','133','133','What should you keep in mind when driving on wet, slushy roads?','[{"key":"a","text":"periodic checking of road adhesion through controlled braking tests"},{"key":"b","text":"periodic cleaning of headlights"},{"key":"c","text":"periodic replacement of windshield wiper blades"},{"key":"d","text":"periodic tire pressure restoration"}]','b','[]'),
